[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mC's determinism there is an artifact of our own call pattern (the previous [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m frame's proxy is still on the stack), not a property of the C program. Documenting the UB boundary explicitly:[0m[0m
[?25l[0m[0mI'll create the following file: [38;5;141m/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-4p7pmr/translation/NOTES-ub.md[0m[38;5;244m (using tool: write)[0m
Purpose: Document UB boundaries and translation choices

[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # Undefined behaviour in the C source, and how the Rust build handles it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/src/lib.c` validates nothing. Three inputs reachable through its public
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m API make the C read or write memory it never initialised or never owned. For
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m those, "byte-identical output" is not a defined target — the C has no defined
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m output. This file records each case, what was measured, and the deliberate
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m choice made in the Rust translation.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## 1. `c2GJK` with an out-of-range `C2_TYPE` (`ERRORS.md` row 36)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;` as plain stack locals and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2MakeProxy`'s `switch` has **no `default:` label**. An invalid `type`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m therefore leaves the proxy completely uninitialised, and `c2GJK` then reads
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `pA.count` (feeding `c2Support`'s loop bound) and `pA.verts[...]`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Measured (`tests/error_paths.rs::probe_c_gjk_bad_type_child`, isolated in a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m child process): the C returns `dist = 0, iterations = 2` for all 24 invalid
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m type values tried — but only because our own harness calls `c2GJK` in a tight
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m loop, so the stack slot still holds the *previous* call's proxy. Any other
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m caller leaves something else there. Agreement with Rust: **0/24**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Choice:** Rust uses `c2Proxy::default()` (zeroed). This is deterministic and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m memory-safe, and for every *valid* type it is overwritten in full by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2MakeProxy`, so it changes nothing on any defined path. Replicating the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m would require reading uninitialised Rust stack — UB in Rust, exploitable by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m LLVM, and it would still only coincide for one specific call pattern.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The differential test therefore asserts:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * both libraries **return** (the C side isolated in a child process so a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   segfault cannot take the suite down), and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * the Rust result is **deterministic** across repeated identical calls.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## 2. Caller-supplied `c2GJKCache` indices (`ERRORS.md` row 26)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2GJK` reads `cache->iA[i]` for `i < cache->count` out of an `int[3]`, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `pA.verts[iA]` out of a `c2v[8]`, with no validation. Three regimes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | regime | C behaviour | Rust behaviour | tested how |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |--------|-------------|----------------|-----------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `count` 1..=3, `iA`/`iB` 4..=7 | in bounds of `verts[8]` but never written by `c2MakeProxy` → uninitialised stack (measured 39/272 samples differ, `tests/probe_ub.rs`) | reads the zeroed slot | Rust must return **deterministically**; values not compared |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `iA >= 8` | reads past `c2Proxy::verts` into adjacent stack | same (raw pointer read) | isolated child process |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `count > 3` | write loop `verts + i` overruns `c2Simplex`'s four `c2sv` slots and corrupts the caller's frame | same | isolated child process — **reliably SIGSEGV in both** |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Choice that mattered:** the Rust translation originally used bounds-checked
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m indexing (`pA.verts[iA as usize]`, `cache->iA[i as usize]`, `saveA[i as usize]`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m That turned a C out-of-bounds *read* into a Rust **panic**, and because these
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m functions are `extern "C"` a panic cannot unwind — it calls `abort()` and kills
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the host process. Aborting the caller is a far larger divergence from C than
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reading an adjacent stack word. All such accesses were converted to raw pointer
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m arithmetic so the Rust build degrades the same way C does. See the comment at
