[38;5;252m[1m## Two real bugs found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The important one came out of a UB probe rather than a happy-path test. The Rust translation used [1mbounds-checked indexing[22m on values a caller supplies in [38;5;10mc2GJKCache[0m ([38;5;10mpA.verts[iA][0m, [38;5;10mcache->iA[i][0m, [38;5;10msaveA[i][0m). C reads out of bounds there; Rust panicked — and since these are [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m, the panic cannot unwind, so it called [38;5;10mabort()[0m and killed the host process. Converting those to raw pointer arithmetic makes Rust degrade the way C does. This is only observable in [38;5;10m--release[0m ([38;5;10mpanic = "abort"[0m), which is why the release run matters.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The second: the [38;5;10mnan_strict[0m suite initially failed on [38;5;10mc2Dot[0m/[38;5;10mc2Det2[0m. That turned out [1mnot[22m to be a translation bug — I verified the same C source produces [38;5;10m0xffc00000[0m at [38;5;10m-O0[0m and [38;5;10m0x7fc00000[0m at [38;5;10m-O2[0m, because x86 propagates the [3mdestination[23m operand when both are NaN and GCC picks the opposite register from LLVM. Matching [38;5;10m-O0[0m byte-for-byte would require writing the Rust operands backwards and would then diverge from an optimised build of the same C. So NaN payloads are canonicalised, and everything order-*independent* is still compared with full bit equality (single-NaN propagation, [38;5;10minf-inf[0m, [38;5;10m0*inf[0m, [38;5;10m±0[0m, subnormals). Documented in [38;5;10mNOTES-nan.md[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Where "byte-identical" is not defined[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Three inputs make the C read memory it never initialised, so it has no defined output to match. Each is measured, not assumed, and documented in [38;5;10mNOTES-ub.md[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- Invalid [38;5;10mC2_TYPE[0m into [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m — [38;5;10mc2MakeProxy[0m has no [38;5;10mdefault:[0m, leaving [38;5;10mc2Proxy[0m uninitialised. Measured agreement 0/24; C's apparent determinism is an artifact of our own call loop leaving the previous proxy on the stack.[0m[0m
- Cache indices past the shape's vertex count — 39/272 samples differ (uninitialised slot).[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcache->count > 3[0m — overruns [38;5;10mc2Simplex[0m and [1mreliably SIGSEGVs in both[22m libraries.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C side of these runs in a spawned child process so a crash can't take the suite down; that is what the 3 [38;5;10mignored[0m tests are. They are isolated probes invoked by their parent tests, not skipped coverage.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
