[0m[0m
I ran the whole suite against C libraries built at [38;5;10m-O1[0m, [38;5;10m-O2[0m, [38;5;10m-O3[0m and [38;5;10m-Os[0m (built into [38;5;10m/tmp[0m, [38;5;10mc_src/[0m untouched) via the harness's [38;5;10mC_SO_PATH[0m override. All pass, so the translation isn't tuned to one codegen. [38;5;10mclang[0m wasn't available for a cross-compiler check.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One measured claim worth flagging: the [38;5;10mwhile (iter < 20)[0m cap is [1mnot reachable[22m through the public API — over 60,000 randomised configurations the histogram is [38;5;10m{0: 25149, 1: 30460, 2: 3938, 3: 453}[0m, because the [38;5;10mhit[0m, duplicate-support and [38;5;10md1 > d0[0m guards always fire first. The test asserts C and Rust agree on the count and that it stays in [38;5;10m0..=20[0m rather than pretending to hit the cap.[0m[0m
